      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 3245461156,
          "type": null,
          "body": "thank you!!, i have updated dict_command_t to use g_new0() as well. In ddictionary_process_command(), the 'code' field is only assigned when the XML attribute is present. If it is missing, the field remains uninitialized when using g_new(), which can lead to undefined behavior when accessed later, Using g_new0() ensures the structure is safely initialized even when optional attributes are absent.",
          "author": {
            "id": 34632063,
            "username": "aamogh82",
            "public_email": null,
            "name": "Amogh Amogh",
            "state": "active",
